# Who must review changes to safety-critical paths.
#
# This is a one-owner project, so every path maps to the owner. Be clear about what that means: GitHub enforces
# CODEOWNERS only through pull requests plus branch protection ("Require review from Code Owners"). Commits are pushed
# straight to main by the auto-push hook, so this file is documentation until that protection is switched on.
# What enforces approval today is config/approvals.yaml (hash-bound, checked at startup) and the tests.
